{"id":952,"date":"2024-12-14T16:01:22","date_gmt":"2024-12-14T03:01:22","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/he-zhang.com\/?page_id=952"},"modified":"2024-12-15T20:22:38","modified_gmt":"2024-12-15T07:22:38","slug":"portfolio","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/he-zhang.com\/portfolio\/","title":{"rendered":"Portfolio"},"content":{"rendered":"\n\n\t<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\"\/>\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"\/>\n  <title>Dynamic Portfolio<\/title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\"\/>\n<\/head>\n<body>\n    <!-- Section Title -->\n    <h2>Human-AI Collaboration<\/h2>\n    \n    <!-- Portfolio Grid -->\n      <!-- Portfolio Item 1 -->\n      Redefining qualitative analysis in the AI era: Utilizing ChatGPT for efficient thematic analysis addresses a growing challenge in qualitative research: the time-intensive and cognitively demanding nature of manual data analysis. As qualitative datasets grow larger and more complex, traditional methods often fall short in efficiency and scalability. This research is motivated by the potential of Large Language Models (LLMs) like ChatGPT to transform qualitative analysis by offering new ways to process and interpret data. By exploring how LLMs can complement human researchers in conducting thematic analysis, the study aims to bridge the gap between computational power and nuanced human understanding, ensuring that qualitative research remains relevant and impactful in the AI era.\n        **Methods**:  \n        (Data Preparation): Semi-structured interview, Co-design.\n        (Human-AI Collaboration): Researchers evaluated ChatGPT&#8217;s outputs through a participatory process, comparing them against human-coded themes. Adjustments and refinements were made to ensure alignment with qualitative standards.\n        (Evaluation and Validation): Participants&#8217; interview feedback.\n        (Iterative Refinement): Insights from evaluations were used to improve the prompting strategy, establishing a replicable framework for LLM-assisted thematic analysis.\n        **Contributions**: \n        **(Framework for LLM-Assisted Thematic Analysis)**: The study proposes a systematic approach to leveraging ChatGPT for thematic analysis, highlighting the model&#8217;s ability to identify and refine themes efficiently.\n        **(Insights on Human-AI Collaboration)**: The research reveals how researchers can work synergistically with LLMs, emphasizing the importance of iterative prompting and critical evaluation to maintain the rigor of qualitative inquiry.\n        **(Discussion of Ethical and Methodological)**: The study raises important discussions about the implications of integrating AI into qualitative research, including issues of bias, transparency, and researcher accountability.\n        &#8221;\n        data-image=&#8221;https:\/\/arxiv.org\/html\/2309.10771v3\/extracted\/5625034\/graph\/workflow.png&#8221; \n        data-links=&#8221;<a href='https:\/\/arxiv.org\/pdf\/2309.10771' target='_blank' rel=\"noopener\">arXiv<\/a>&#8220;>\n        <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/he-zhang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/AItool3.webp\" alt=\"Project 1\"\/>\n        <h3>LLMs Support Human Work<\/h3>\n      <!-- Portfolio Item 2 -->\n      QualiGPT addresses a critical bottleneck in qualitative research-the time-consuming and complex nature of the coding process. Existing qualitative analysis tools often lack automation, user-friendliness, and cost efficiency, limiting their accessibility to researchers. The emergence of Large Language Models (LLMs), such as GPT-3 and its successors, offers promising capabilities for enhancing qualitative analysis workflows. Motivated by this opportunity, this study introduces QualiGPT, a tool designed to leverage LLMs for efficient and transparent qualitative coding. By comparing manual coding with QualiGPT across both simulated and real-world datasets, the research highlights how AI can improve efficiency, accessibility, and transparency in qualitative research.\n        **Methods**:  \n        **(Tool Development)**: The QualiGPT was developed using ChatGPT APIs, with carefully designed prompts tailored to thematic analysis tasks.\n        **(Dataset Selection)**: The real-world qualitative dataset was utilized.\n        **(Coding Process)**: **Inductive Coding**: QualiGPT was used to identify themes without a predefined codebook, mimicking exploratory qualitative analysis. **Deductive Coding**: Predefined codebooks were provided to assess the tool&#8217;s ability to apply existing coding frameworks.\n        **(Performance Evaluation)** Consistency between human coders and QualiGPT was quantified using inter-rater reliability (IRR) metrics, such as Fleiss&#8217; Kappa.\n        **(Result Analysis)**  A comparative analysis was conducted to evaluate the efficiency, accuracy, and usability of QualiGPT against traditional manual coding approaches.\n        **Discussion**: \n        **(Enhancing Researcher Efficiency)**: One of the core discussions centers around how LLMs, like ChatGPT, can alleviate the time-intensive nature of qualitative coding. The study highlights that while AI-powered tools can significantly accelerate coding tasks, their outputs require careful validation to ensure alignment with the nuances of qualitative methodologies.\n        **(Balancing Automation and Human Expertise)**: The research underscores the complementary roles of AI and human researchers. While QualiGPT can identify themes and patterns efficiently, human input remains essential to interpret context-sensitive data, refine outputs, and address areas where the model may lack cultural or domain-specific understanding.\n        **(Ethical Implications)**: The study raises ethical considerations about the use of LLMs in research, including the risks of bias in AI-generated outputs and the potential for over-reliance on automated tools. It suggests the need for transparent reporting of how AI tools are integrated into research workflows to ensure rigor and accountability.\n        **(Scalability in Qualitative Research)**:  The study considers the scalability of LLM-powered tools for handling large datasets. While traditional manual methods often struggle with extensive datasets, QualiGPT&#8217;s efficiency makes it a viable option for scaling qualitative studies, enabling researchers to analyze larger and more complex datasets than previously feasible.\n        **(Future Directions for Human-AI Collaboration)**: The paper closes with a reflection on how the role of qualitative researchers may evolve as AI tools become more prevalent. Rather than replacing human expertise, AI can augment the researcher&#8217;s capabilities, enabling them to focus on higher-order interpretative and theoretical work.\n        &#8221;\n        data-image=&#8221;https:\/\/he-zhang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/qualigpt.jpg&#8221; \n        data-images=&#8221;https:\/\/arxiv.org\/html\/2407.14925v1\/extracted\/5744773\/graph\/QualiGPT-teaserfigure.png, https:\/\/arxiv.org\/html\/2407.14925v1\/extracted\/5744773\/graph\/Instruction-Manual.png&#8221;\n        data-links=&#8221;<a href='https:\/\/arxiv.org\/pdf\/2309.10771' target='_blank' rel=\"noopener\">arXiv<\/a>, <a href='https:\/\/github.com\/KindOPSTAR\/QualiGPT' target='_blank' rel=\"noopener\">Github<\/a>&#8220;>\n        <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/he-zhang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/AItool.webp\" alt=\"Project 2\"\/>\n        <h3>AI Toolkit, Prototype &#038; Plugin <\/h3>\n      <!-- Portfolio Item 3 -->\n      Full Paper&#8221;>\n        <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/he-zhang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/Education.webp\" alt=\"Project 3\"\/>\n        <h3>LLMs x Education<\/h3>\n    <!-- Expanded Details -->\n     <button>&times;<\/button>\n     <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"\" alt=\"Details Image\"\/>\n    